      "projects": [
        {
          "title": "Chord Peer-to-Peer Network Protocol ",
          "subtitle": "Nov 2018 - Nov 2018",
          "subComponenets": [
            {
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "Associated with University of Florida"
                },
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "Chord is a protocol and algorithm for a peer-to-peer distributed hash table. A distributed hash table stores key-value pairs by assigning keys to different computers (known as \"nodes\"); a node will store the values for all the keys for which it is responsible. Chord specifies how keys are assigned to nodes, and how a node can discover the value for a given key by first locating the node responsible for that key. The SHA-1 algorithm is the base hashing function for consistent hashing.Actor Model was designed to perform various operations of the Chord Protocol that includes - creating a network of nodes, joining nodes, stabilizing the protocol and updated the finger tables of the nodes in the network."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Gossip Algorithm",
          "subtitle": "Oct 2018 - Oct 2018",
          "subComponenets": [
            {
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "Associated with University of Florida"
                },
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "Gossip Algorithm is used for information propagation The Gossip algorithm involves the following:\n1.)Starting: A participant(actor) it told/sent a rumor(fact) by the main process.\n2.)Step: Each actor selects a random neighbor and tells it the rumor.\n3.) Termination: Each actor keeps track of rumors and how many times it has heard the rumor. It stops transmitting once it has heard the rumor 10 times.Gossip type algorithms can be used both for group communication and for aggregate computation.Implemented randomized gossip algorithm for information exchange in distributed network in Elixir. Push sum was implemented in similar fashion. Analysis was done on 6 topologies ."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Lucas Square Pyramid",
          "subtitle": "Sep 2018 - Sep 2018",
          "subComponenets": [
            {
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "Associated with University of Florida"
                },
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "The project is based on the interesting problem of elliptic curve theory , the problem of finding the perfect squares that are sums of consecutive squares. A classic example is the Pythagorean identity:\n3^2 + 4^2 = 5^2.\nthat reveals that the sum of squares of 3 and 4 is itself a square. A more interesting\nexample is Lucas` Square Pyramid :\n1^2 + 2^2 + ::: + 24^2 = 70^2 \nIn both of these examples, sums of squares of consecutive integers form the\nsquare of another integer.A concurrent algorithm in Elixir using Actor model was developed for achieving a parallelism of 10^6 using light weight processes. Multiple machines were connected in a Master-Slave architecture, to increase parallelism and decrease the computation time for large inputs of the order 10^9. "
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
